{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows early negative signals.",
    "Reduce forecast bias by applying a mean-reversion correction to recent over- or under-forecasted periods.",
    "When price spikes occur, apply a lagged correction: reduce forecast by 10-15% of the spike magnitude after 2-3 days.",
    "For long-term horizons (>10 days), apply a smoothing filter to dampen volatility and avoid overreaction to short-term sentiment shifts.",
    "If sentiment is positive and price is trending downward, increase forecast slightly to counteract mean reversion bias.",
    "When true outcome is consistently below forecast, especially after a spike, apply a downward bias correction of 5-8% to avoid overestimating rebound potential."
  ]
}
